    "done_when": "TelemetryIndex.ingest no longer commits each sample in its own transaction: _insert stops opening a transaction per row, and ingest commits after a bounded batch of rows (a module constant, with ingest accepting a batch_rows keyword for tests) together with the source row, advancing that source's offset, size, mtime and prefix digest to the end of the last committed line at each batch, so a pass killed mid-source resumes at the last committed batch and re-reads no committed row; the deselected-tier drop and the rebuilt-in-place handling behave as before; tests in tests/test_telemetry_index.py assert, using sqlite3's set_trace_callback to count COMMIT statements, that ingesting a 1000-row fixture source with batch_rows 250 issues at most 6 commits; that an ingest made to raise after its second batch leaves the source offset at the end of the second batch's last line and a second ingest completes the file with every row stored once and no duplicate counted; and that the prefix digest after a batched ingest equals the digest an unbatched read of the same bytes records; measured on the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), never the login node: cold-ingest the first 20 MB of /work/projects/imas_gpu/agents/receipts/deepseek-v4-1-flash-1273253.jsonl (copied, cut at a line end) into a fresh index under ~/.cache/ambix-batch-measure/ at the base revision and at the head, recording rows per second and wall time for each in /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/0c4316b2-553f-4a0a-ae02-c42d88de747c/srw-ingest-commits-in-batches/measure.md, then delete that scratch directory; gate: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_telemetry_index.py tests/test_telemetry_ingest.py tests/test_agent_telemetry_watch.py passes, pytest tests/test_agent_serve_registry.py -k agent_package_modules_parse_with_serving_python passes, uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0; the gate log's first line names the commit it ran at and each command's exit status is recorded as EXIT=0 or the non-zero status",
